        {
          "id": "69c18341f12040402a36284e",
          "question": "<p>Find the multiplication of numbers whose base value 100.</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>101</mn><mo>&times;</mo><mn>109</mn><mo>=</mo></math></p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>11001</p>",
            "<p>11009</p>",
            "<p>11109</p>",
            "<p>11079</p>",
            "<p>11709</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>101</mn><mo>&times;</mo><mn>109</mn></math></p>\n<p>Multiplying numbers close to 100 is efficient using the base 100 method,</p>\n<p>Subtract 100 from each number to get the deviation,</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>101</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>\n<p>Subtract 100 from each number to get the deviation,</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>109</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p>\n<p>Add the base (100) to one number's deviation or simply add the deviations of the two numbers to 100,</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>101</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>110</mn></math> (Left part)</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&times;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math> (Right part)</p>\n<p>Left part: 110</p>\n<p>Right part: 09 (as it needs two digits for the base 100).</p>\n<p>Final result: 11009</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "69c18341f12040402a362840",
          "question": "<p>Find the multiplication of numbers whose base value 100.</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>98</mn><mo>&times;</mo><mn>99</mn><mo>=</mo></math></p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>9700</p>",
            "<p>9802</p>",
            "<p>9902</p>",
            "<p>9702</p>",
            "<p>9602</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 3,
          "explanation": "<p>Identify deviations from the base (100)</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>98</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mn>99</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>\n<p>Perform two calculations:</p>\n<p>Left part:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>98</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>97</mn></math></p>\n<p>Right part:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&times;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>\n<p>Left part: 97</p>\n<p>Right part: 02 (as it needs two digits for the base 100)</p>\n<p>Final result: 9702</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "69c18341f12040402a362857",
          "question": "<p>Find the multiplication of any three digit numbers.</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>204</mn><mo>&times;</mo><mn>206</mn><mo>=</mo></math></p>",
          "image_url": null,
