          ],
          "correct": 0,
          "explanation": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The digits of 8464 are paired as 84 64.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The unit digit of 8464 is 4. Hence, the possible unit digits, after taking the square root could be 2 and 8.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Let us consider the pair of digits 84.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The number 84 lies between two perfect squares 81 and 100 that is,&nbsp; 81&lt; 84 &lt; 100 which can be written as </span><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&lt;84&lt;</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> =&nbsp; </span><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>84</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Hence, the tens digit of the square root of 8464 is 9 since 9&lt;10</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As the number obtained above is 2 and 8. The numbers can be 92 or 98.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The product of the possible tens digit gives the value 90 (as here a = 9 and b = 10).</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As 84 &lt; 90, the square root of 8464 will be 92.</span></p>"
        },
