          "explanation": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The digits of 4624 are paired as 46 24.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The unit digit of 4624 is 4. Hence, the possible unit digits, after taking the square root could be 2 and 8.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Let us consider the pair of digits 46.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The number 46 lies between two perfect squares 36 and 49 that is,&nbsp; 36 &lt; 46 &lt; 49 which can be written as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>46</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>46</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Hence, the tens digit of the square root of 4624 is 6 since 6&lt;7.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As the number obtained above is 2 and 8. The numbers can be 62 or 68.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The product of the possible tens digit gives the value 42 (as here a = 6 and b = 7).</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As 42 &lt; 46, the square root of 4624 will be the greater of 62 which is 68.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"
